WEBVTT

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.000
[This is a fictional story. All characters and events bear no relation to reality]

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.000
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.033
[under the guardian and expert supervision per guidelines]

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:40.033
[Episode 4]

00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:48.816
[Durumi Electronics Sales Team Workshop]

00:00:51.932 --> 00:00:55.083
- Hey, Manager Lee. Get me a latte. - Okay.

00:01:00.622 --> 00:01:02.476
Mr. Han!

00:01:02.476 --> 00:01:05.632
Hey, not sure if you remember.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.648
But we made a bet yesterday while drinking.

00:01:07.648 --> 00:01:11.360
The first one to pass out had to buy snacks at the rest area.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.092
Mr. Bong.

00:01:13.092 --> 00:01:14.792
Team Leader Bong.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.749
Here you go.

00:01:17.749 --> 00:01:20.240
Oh, thank you, Mr. Han.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.732
I'll go easy on your card.

00:01:22.732 --> 00:01:25.292
No, just go all out.

00:01:25.292 --> 00:01:26.549
Just go big. Go big.

00:01:26.549 --> 00:01:29.949
All right, I'll go big.

00:01:31.068 --> 00:01:34.316
Everyone, let's go eat!

00:01:34.952 --> 00:01:36.820
What's with me?

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.116
Why am I scared of him?

00:02:04.852 --> 00:02:08.516
What? Did I dream something last night?

00:02:10.349 --> 00:02:12.472
Oh, my, I have heartburn.

00:02:12.472 --> 00:02:15.883
Oh, why does my shoulder hurt so much?

00:02:16.664 --> 00:02:18.616
Oh, dear, my neck.

00:02:19.508 --> 00:02:21.084
- Director Yoo! - What?

00:02:21.084 --> 00:02:23.656
Have some of this first.

00:02:23.656 --> 00:02:25.396
A hangover cure?

00:02:25.396 --> 00:02:28.464
I don't get hangovers. You have it.

00:02:28.464 --> 00:02:31.783
Oh, you don't have one.

00:02:32.464 --> 00:02:35.460
You were amazing yesterday, Director.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.940
Why? Did something happen yesterday?

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:41.216
No, nothing.

00:02:44.183 --> 00:02:47.016
Oh, good work.

00:02:47.772 --> 00:02:50.949
It was your first scene, so you were a bit flustered, right?

00:02:52.012 --> 00:02:53.712
You did well.

00:02:54.524 --> 00:02:56.416
Thank you.

00:02:58.384 --> 00:03:01.392
Director, can I ask you something?

00:03:01.392 --> 00:03:02.392
What is it?

00:03:02.392 --> 00:03:04.384
Why'd we handle those guys like that yesterday?

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.600
It was different from other meetings.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.083
Didn't you hear? It was a pre-meeting.

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:29.316
Oh, my back...

00:03:40.012 --> 00:03:41.052
They turned themselves in?

00:03:41.052 --> 00:03:44.183
We got a call at the station as soon as the sun came up.

00:03:44.183 --> 00:03:46.316
The old man said he wanted to surrender.

00:03:46.316 --> 00:03:48.916
And he confessed to everything without even being asked.

00:03:48.916 --> 00:03:50.632
He admitted they harvested the organs

00:03:50.632 --> 00:03:52.283
From all seven missing victims and buried them.

00:03:52.283 --> 00:03:53.904
He even gave them the burial sites.

00:03:53.904 --> 00:03:55.792
He said it all happened in that warehouse.

00:03:55.792 --> 00:03:58.383
The crime scene investigator is currently collecting DNA samples.

00:03:58.383 --> 00:04:01.420
But why are they all in such bad shape?

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.049
Apparently they got into a fight and beat each other up.

00:04:05.049 --> 00:04:06.576
Bad enough to end up like this?

00:04:06.576 --> 00:04:07.920
Well, we can't know the reason

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.583
Because no one will say what they fought over.

00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:11.616
Anyway, that's what they said happened.

00:04:31.316 --> 00:04:32.956
What about recent guests?

00:04:32.956 --> 00:04:34.932
They hadn't been operating for the past month,

00:04:34.932 --> 00:04:36.168
So there were no guests.

00:04:36.168 --> 00:04:37.476
So there wasn't a guest list either.

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:39.464
Did you check the CCTV?

00:04:39.464 --> 00:04:41.688
Oh, well...

00:04:41.688 --> 00:04:45.316
That's the strange part. Nothing's there.

00:04:45.316 --> 00:04:47.744
What do you mean? Was it erased?

00:04:47.744 --> 00:04:49.649
Well, they said they turned it off.

00:04:49.649 --> 00:04:53.328
We don't know whether it was deleted or never existed.

00:04:53.328 --> 00:04:56.588
In 15 years as a detective, I've never had a case handed to me this easily.

00:04:56.588 --> 00:04:59.588
We've got the scene, the evidence, and the confession.

00:04:59.588 --> 00:05:01.483
CCTV or not, it doesn't matter.

00:05:04.268 --> 00:05:06.349
No, just...

00:05:06.349 --> 00:05:10.449
[Inspection in Progress, Reduce Speed]

00:05:16.372 --> 00:05:18.576
Step out of the vehicle.

00:05:18.576 --> 00:05:20.912
I said, step out.

00:05:20.912 --> 00:05:23.280
I told you, it's urgent. That's why we have to hurry.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.160
We're responding to an emergency call.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:28.980
That's why I'm asking you to show me your ID.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.776
Oh, you're really dedicated. Just let us through.

00:05:31.776 --> 00:05:34.549
Come on, where do you think you're going?

00:05:34.549 --> 00:05:35.983
Someone's dying right now.

00:05:35.983 --> 00:05:38.983
I need to perform CPR. Have a good day.

00:05:38.983 --> 00:05:42.449
I understand. Just show me your ID.

00:05:44.682 --> 00:05:45.828
Arrest him! Get him!

00:05:45.828 --> 00:05:47.106
- Show me your ID! Grab him! - Darn it.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.008
Yeah, Beom, what's going on?

00:05:51.008 --> 00:05:53.744
We were checking an ambulance heading towards the pension.

00:05:53.744 --> 00:05:56.949
And the man inside suddenly tried to run, so we caught him.

00:05:56.949 --> 00:06:00.216
He was wearing a doctor's gown. Looks like he's the organ-harvesting surgeon.

00:06:00.216 --> 00:06:02.649
- The surgeon? - Come on. Show me your ID. Hurry up.

00:06:02.649 --> 00:06:05.024
Huh? Get him!

00:06:05.024 --> 00:06:06.768
- Hurry, show me your ID! - Okay.

00:06:06.768 --> 00:06:08.468
What's his name?

00:06:09.156 --> 00:06:10.883
Jo Dong Min?

00:06:10.883 --> 00:06:13.192
It's not Jo Dong Min.

00:06:13.192 --> 00:06:16.616
It's Jo Dong Man. Man.

00:06:18.072 --> 00:06:20.228
He says it's Jo Dong Man. Did you check his ID?

00:06:20.228 --> 00:06:22.760
Mr. Jo here is quite skilled.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.584
So clients are supposed to come once every hour.

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:30.512
Just wait at the entrance to the pension and catch them one by one.

00:06:30.512 --> 00:06:32.212
Got it.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.249
Keep checking vehicles. A buyer's coming every hour.

00:06:45.768 --> 00:06:48.728
<i>Where did all these darn flies come from?</i>

00:06:48.728 --> 00:06:50.428
<i>Flies?</i>

00:06:51.772 --> 00:06:53.816
Die, you punk!

00:07:11.756 --> 00:07:13.783
Get on your knees, you punk!

00:07:18.096 --> 00:07:20.116
<i>Get on your knees, you punk!</i>

00:07:26.516 --> 00:07:28.988
Hey, get on your knees.

00:07:28.988 --> 00:07:30.444
Get on your knees! Hurry!

00:07:30.444 --> 00:07:32.583
Kneel down, you punks!

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.864
Isn't handing them over to the police just a waste of time?

00:07:44.864 --> 00:07:48.049
They won't be properly punished anyway.

00:07:49.424 --> 00:07:50.436
How do you know that?

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:53.840
Whether they'll be punished or not.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:58.300
Do you just distrust and resent the police, the law, and the courts by default?

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:01.449
No, well, not exactly like that, but...

00:08:01.449 --> 00:08:04.916
A pre-meeting means we let the law handle it first.

00:08:04.916 --> 00:08:08.683
It's about respecting its role and responsibility.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:13.123
Of course, the system has its limits.

00:08:13.123 --> 00:08:17.692
Sometimes verdicts result in only minimal punishment.

00:08:17.692 --> 00:08:21.524
And sometimes, those who have no business interfering

00:08:21.524 --> 00:08:24.097
End up obstructing rightful justice.

00:08:24.097 --> 00:08:28.163
But that doesn't mean we should dismiss the system entirely, right?

00:08:28.163 --> 00:08:31.416
We're not trying to create a lawless world, are we?

00:08:33.183 --> 00:08:38.640
I think they do their job, and we do ours.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:42.883
Sometimes we simply do what they cannot.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.716
Director Yoo!

00:08:54.468 --> 00:08:56.328
But then again, who knows.

00:08:56.328 --> 00:09:00.916
Someday, today's pre-meeting might become an official one.

00:09:02.992 --> 00:09:05.316
If they forget about us.

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:15.349
<i>If they forget that there are forces more terrifying than the law.</i>

00:09:20.483 --> 00:09:22.870
[Organ Trafficking Ring Targeting Hikers] <i>A despicable organ trafficking ring</i>

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:24.064
[Busted by Police] <i>that kidnapped hikers,</i>

00:09:24.064 --> 00:09:26.352
<i>harvested their organs, and secretly buried their bodies</i>

00:09:26.352 --> 00:09:28.172
[Mount Taegong Missing Hikers] <i>has been arrested by police.</i>

00:09:28.172 --> 00:09:29.556
[Confirmed Dead] <i>It has been confirmed that</i>

00:09:29.556 --> 00:09:33.042
<i>all of the victims kidnapped and murdered by the organization</i>

00:09:33.042 --> 00:09:34.616
<i>were hikers who had previously been reported missing</i>

00:09:34.616 --> 00:09:38.449
<i>in the recent Mount Taegong serial disappearance case.</i>

00:09:41.412 --> 00:09:43.983
<i>Police stated today that they have recovered all of the victims' bodies,</i>

00:09:43.983 --> 00:09:48.916
<i>which were found buried in secluded mountain areas across the country.</i>

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:51.383
[Illegal Organ Clinic Raided] <i>Police conducted raids on hospitals</i>

00:09:51.383 --> 00:09:54.313
[All Involved Personnel Arrested] <i>that purchased organs from them</i>

00:09:54.313 --> 00:09:59.016
<i>and performed illegal surgeries, and arrested all involved parties.</i>

00:09:59.826 --> 00:10:03.564
<i>The police, having secured a list of illegal organ transplant recipients,</i>

00:10:03.564 --> 00:10:06.908
<i>are expanding their investigation across the entire medical sector.</i>

00:10:06.908 --> 00:10:09.426
<i>Authorities are also launching a full-scale crackdown</i>

00:10:09.426 --> 00:10:11.184
<i>on illegal organ trafficking</i>

00:10:11.184 --> 00:10:14.288
<i>and pursuing other institutions involved in similar crimes,</i>

00:10:14.288 --> 00:10:17.783
<i>ensuring those responsible face the full extent of the law.</i>

00:10:18.808 --> 00:10:21.483
<i>I hope they remember.</i>

00:10:21.483 --> 00:10:24.162
<i>Those who take their crimes lightly and disregard the law</i>

00:10:24.162 --> 00:10:28.349
<i>should remember that the harshest punishment comes for them</i>

00:10:28.349 --> 00:10:32.316
<i>when they feel the safest and most at ease.</i>

00:10:48.816 --> 00:10:53.972
Oh, I see. So you support Kingfisher? Got it.

00:10:53.972 --> 00:10:55.912
I understand your opinion.

00:10:55.912 --> 00:11:01.016
But as police officers, we have a duty to stay true to our responsibilities.

00:11:03.684 --> 00:11:05.568
No, he said it was a tip-off call, but instead of giving me anything,

00:11:05.568 --> 00:11:07.692
He just told me outright not to catch Kingfisher.

00:11:07.692 --> 00:11:10.100
Oh, seriously...

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.332
Hey, don't even mention it.

00:11:11.332 --> 00:11:13.416
Every time a major crime happens,

00:11:13.416 --> 00:11:15.760
People act like Kingfisher is some kind of hero.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:19.412
Jeez, it's so distracting that I can barely work.

00:11:19.412 --> 00:11:22.420
At most, it'll be another month or two.

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:24.816
Something else will happen somewhere soon, won't it?

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.212
- Make sure the team leader eats well. - Okay.

00:11:28.212 --> 00:11:29.985
We're heading out for a stakeout in Inseong-dong.

00:11:29.985 --> 00:11:31.983
- Good luck. - Yes, sir!

00:11:31.983 --> 00:11:33.448
[Violent Crimes Team 2]

00:11:33.448 --> 00:11:35.149
Take care.

00:11:38.424 --> 00:11:40.788
It's already this late...

00:11:40.788 --> 00:11:42.972
Should we order dinner?

00:11:42.972 --> 00:11:44.928
The victims.

00:11:44.928 --> 00:11:46.908
Pardon?

00:11:46.908 --> 00:11:50.749
When the perpetrator's side is blocked, break through the victim's side.

00:11:51.988 --> 00:11:55.288
So far, Kingfisher's crime intervals ranged from 7 to 60 days.

00:11:55.288 --> 00:11:58.583
Like Mr. Jang said, another one will happen somewhere soon.

00:11:58.583 --> 00:12:00.558
What if we chase the case

00:12:00.558 --> 00:12:03.596
That's going to happen instead of the one that's already happened?

00:12:03.596 --> 00:12:05.676
The case that's going to happen?

00:12:05.676 --> 00:12:07.668
Kingfisher's next target.

00:12:07.668 --> 00:12:10.516
The next target? Who is it?

00:12:14.424 --> 00:12:15.800
No, I don't want to go.

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.288
Why?

00:12:17.288 --> 00:12:20.283
You're going to a kids' cafe with daycare today.

00:12:20.283 --> 00:12:21.624
It's going to be so much fun, isn't it?

00:12:21.624 --> 00:12:23.528
Mommy isn't coming.

00:12:23.528 --> 00:12:26.912
Yul, I told you I have to go to work today, so I can't, right?

00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:27.976
That's right, Yul.

00:12:27.976 --> 00:12:30.268
Mommy has to go to work today, so she can't go.

00:12:30.268 --> 00:12:34.372
Instead, I will buy you new Baby Shark stickers tonight. Okay?

00:12:34.372 --> 00:12:36.583
No, don't buy me any.

00:12:38.444 --> 00:12:40.908
This won't do. Honey, you go ahead.

00:12:40.908 --> 00:12:42.896
You said you have to leave early for a local assignment today. Hurry.

00:12:42.896 --> 00:12:44.296
It's still fine.

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:46.676
We're going to get right up, right, Yul?

00:12:46.676 --> 00:12:48.472
No, I won't get up.

00:12:48.472 --> 00:12:49.508
Kwon Yul.

00:12:49.508 --> 00:12:52.264
If you don't get up by the time I count to five,

00:12:52.264 --> 00:12:55.375
I'll pick you up myself and take you out.

00:12:55.375 --> 00:12:56.808
Do you want me to do that?

00:12:56.808 --> 00:12:58.352
No, don't!

00:12:58.352 --> 00:12:59.724
I'm counting.

00:12:59.724 --> 00:13:02.983
One, two...

00:13:02.983 --> 00:13:05.389
So scary. You should get up quickly, Yul.

00:13:05.389 --> 00:13:07.749
You know Mommy doesn't go easy on you when she's mad, right?

00:13:10.716 --> 00:13:12.516
Three!

00:13:12.516 --> 00:13:14.832
Here it comes, four!

00:13:14.832 --> 00:13:18.283
Hmph, Mommy, no mercy!

00:13:24.244 --> 00:13:25.944
No mercy...

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:34.092
My daughter is so smart.

00:13:34.092 --> 00:13:35.583
Give it to me.

00:13:35.583 --> 00:13:39.588
See? Mommy really doesn't go easy on you.

00:13:39.588 --> 00:13:43.636
She's been that merciless since way back.

00:13:43.636 --> 00:13:48.316
When Daddy first met Mommy, she was really scary.

00:13:49.423 --> 00:13:51.208
So scary. Let's go.

00:13:51.208 --> 00:13:53.349
So scary!

00:13:56.444 --> 00:14:00.916
Yul, what did Mommy tell you to do at the kids' cafe today?

00:14:00.916 --> 00:14:01.916
Huh?

00:14:01.916 --> 00:14:05.683
Listen to your teacher. Don't fight with your friends.

00:14:05.683 --> 00:14:08.716
And be careful not to get hurt, okay?

00:14:08.716 --> 00:14:11.292
That's what you need to do, got it? Okay?

00:14:11.292 --> 00:14:15.440
Oh? It's Seo Jun! Mommy, it's Seo Jun!

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:17.867
- No. - No, I...

00:14:17.867 --> 00:14:18.944
Huh?

00:14:18.944 --> 00:14:20.316
- I won't go. - I'm late.

00:14:20.316 --> 00:14:23.016
I'm late. Let's go quickly.

00:14:24.024 --> 00:14:27.649
My car went in for repairs yesterday.

00:14:29.788 --> 00:14:32.644
I couldn't even get a taxi.

00:14:32.644 --> 00:14:35.244
My kid just picked today to throw a fit about not wanting to go to daycare.

00:14:35.244 --> 00:14:37.324
You must have been at a loss.

00:14:37.324 --> 00:14:41.768
They say four is the difficult age. That's exactly how my kid's been lately.

00:14:41.768 --> 00:14:43.944
Every morning is a battle.

00:14:43.944 --> 00:14:47.012
My commute is already a battle since my office is so far away.

00:14:47.012 --> 00:14:49.120
My mommy goes to work too, right?

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:51.012
That's right, Yul.

00:14:51.012 --> 00:14:53.156
Do you work too?

00:14:53.156 --> 00:14:57.416
I was on parental leave and just recently returned to work.

00:14:57.416 --> 00:14:58.492
I'm just getting back into it.

00:14:58.492 --> 00:15:01.488
Oh, I didn't know.

00:15:01.488 --> 00:15:04.416
My mommy isn't coming to the kids' cafe.

00:15:05.037 --> 00:15:06.954
Right, Yul?

00:15:06.954 --> 00:15:10.649
It must be especially hard since you've only just gone back.

00:15:11.488 --> 00:15:12.924
After staying home with kids every day,

00:15:12.924 --> 00:15:16.849
Going back to work must have you feeling up and down lately, right?

00:15:17.816 --> 00:15:20.616
When you're just at home, you miss the outside world.

00:15:20.616 --> 00:15:22.777
And when you're actually out working, you worry about the child you left behind.

00:15:22.777 --> 00:15:24.149
Do you feel that way too?

00:15:24.149 --> 00:15:26.283
Oh, I was even worse.

00:15:26.283 --> 00:15:29.392
I had to leave my baby when he was barely a year old.

00:15:29.392 --> 00:15:32.464
So days like today make me feel especially guilty.

00:15:32.464 --> 00:15:35.116
The other moms all volunteer to go.

00:15:35.116 --> 00:15:36.688
I hate you, Mommy!

00:15:36.688 --> 00:15:38.000
Park Seo Jun.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:41.156
You shouldn't say such mean things to your mommy.

00:15:41.156 --> 00:15:42.744
Funny, isn't it?

00:15:42.744 --> 00:15:44.414
I hate you, Mommy.

00:15:44.414 --> 00:15:46.608
Do you hate Mommy too, Yul?

00:15:46.608 --> 00:15:50.060
I'm sorry. What can I do?

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:53.083
- I'd better get going. - See you later, Ma'am.

00:15:55.644 --> 00:15:57.272
Why are they suddenly walking in together?

00:15:57.272 --> 00:16:00.728
Moms have to stick together and look out for each other.

00:16:00.728 --> 00:16:01.808
How are you?

00:16:01.808 --> 00:16:03.980
Oh, hello.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.559
Hello, Miss.

00:16:05.559 --> 00:16:08.400
Oh, Seo Jun and Yul came together today?

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:11.083
Hello, Miss.

00:16:12.956 --> 00:16:14.976
Hey, you!

00:16:14.976 --> 00:16:16.458
I'm sorry, Miss.

00:16:16.458 --> 00:16:18.538
It's okay.

00:16:18.538 --> 00:16:20.750
Please take good care of him today as well.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.276
Yul's mom, thank you so much today.

00:16:24.276 --> 00:16:25.316
I'll send you a coffee coupon.

00:16:25.316 --> 00:16:26.383
No, it's fine.

00:16:26.383 --> 00:16:28.849
- I'll get going first. - Okay, take care.

00:16:28.849 --> 00:16:31.056
Yul, aren't you going to say bye to Mommy?

00:16:31.056 --> 00:16:32.410
Okay. My Yul.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:34.726
Today, too, with your friends, get along well...

