Oh, dear, seriously.

00:34:37.572 --> 00:34:39.052
You sure have a lot of free time.

00:34:39.052 --> 00:34:41.972
If you don't trust us, you can just not get in!

00:34:41.972 --> 00:34:43.849
I won't go either then.

00:34:43.849 --> 00:34:45.949
Oh, my.

00:34:45.949 --> 00:34:50.016
No, I mean, Mr. Park offered good money

00:34:50.016 --> 00:34:53.442
And kept insisting that he had to leave today.

00:34:53.442 --> 00:34:55.620
So I even canceled my own meeting and came all the way here.

00:34:55.620 --> 00:34:58.729
And I even brought an expert who can remove the ankle monitor.

00:34:58.729 --> 00:35:00.036
This ankle monitor?

00:35:00.036 --> 00:35:04.316
Oh, dear, not just anyone can remove it. It's darn difficult!

00:35:05.416 --> 00:35:09.696
Fine, then stay here and wait around until the police catch you.

00:35:09.696 --> 00:35:12.009
That's none of my business, okay?

00:35:12.009 --> 00:35:16.620
And you do know that if the client refuses,

00:35:16.620 --> 00:35:19.497
Refunds are absolutely impossible, right? Huh?

00:35:19.497 --> 00:35:22.080
You're way too suspicious.

00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:24.300
Hey, what are you doing? Get in the car. I'm going home.

00:35:24.300 --> 00:35:26.116
We shouldn't have come here.

00:35:35.640 --> 00:35:39.842
Oh, dear, anyway, you picked a darn good day.

00:35:39.842 --> 00:35:44.072
This is exactly the kind of weather that's perfect for leaving.

00:35:44.072 --> 00:35:47.516
Let's stop by the neighborhood before we leave.

00:35:47.516 --> 00:35:53.064
What? Your house will be crawling with people right now.

00:35:53.064 --> 00:35:57.087
If you go there, you'll see things you shouldn't see.

00:35:57.087 --> 00:35:59.516
Who says I'm going home?

00:36:00.126 --> 00:36:03.689
Well, then where?

00:36:03.689 --> 00:36:08.983
Before leaving for a long journey, I should at least see the kid's face once.

00:36:10.104 --> 00:36:14.144
I'm curious how much she's grown.

00:36:14.144 --> 00:36:19.516
She was about eight back then, so after more than ten years...

00:36:20.865 --> 00:36:24.083
Wow, she must be all grown up into a young lady.

00:36:32.472 --> 00:36:34.949
Do you really have to go that far?

00:36:49.516 --> 00:36:51.449
Manager Tae, nice!

00:36:55.177 --> 00:36:56.940
Oh, dear, he looks comfortable.

00:36:56.940 --> 00:36:59.016
Let's switch back again.

00:37:01.240 --> 00:37:04.183
Oh, dear, I guess I'm just not suited for big cars.

00:37:20.746 --> 00:37:22.804
I've been wondering about something.

00:37:22.804 --> 00:37:25.664
Why do you use such complicated methods, like staged accidents?

00:37:25.664 --> 00:37:28.148
It would be easier to just have Kingfisher shoot them once.

00:37:28.148 --> 00:37:32.148
That would work, but there are too many to handle alone.

00:37:32.148 --> 00:37:36.883
Especially since we're in charge of the 'white' cases.

00:37:36.883 --> 00:37:39.396
White...

00:37:39.396 --> 00:37:41.696
Why?

00:37:41.696 --> 00:37:44.516
A single shot, without pain, clean and simple.

00:37:44.516 --> 00:37:46.116
That's Bo Na's way.

00:37:46.116 --> 00:37:48.120
I know that much.

00:37:48.120 --> 00:37:51.083
One shot, one kill. Kingfisher's signature move.

00:37:51.083 --> 00:37:53.216
Do you know why that is?

00:37:53.216 --> 00:37:54.916
Well, that's because...

00:37:55.976 --> 00:37:57.716
She's good at it?

00:37:59.644 --> 00:38:01.316
I think the driver must've gotten sleepy.

00:38:01.316 --> 00:38:02.580
[Drowsy Driving Rest Area]

00:38:02.580 --> 00:38:04.349
You should hurry.

00:38:13.860 --> 00:38:15.560
This is the truck.

00:38:17.820 --> 00:38:19.340
Beom, check the top.

00:38:19.340 --> 00:38:21.040
Yes.

00:38:27.283 --> 00:38:29.250
Jeez. Oh, dear!

00:38:30.660 --> 00:38:32.049
This is the police!

00:38:32.049 --> 00:38:34.416
Stay where you are and please cooperate.

00:38:38.250 --> 00:38:39.324
Darn it!

00:38:47.448 --> 00:38:49.572
Oh, that scared me.

00:38:49.572 --> 00:38:51.849
I thought it was a dismembered body.

00:39:06.136 --> 00:39:10.649
After all this, they just roughly dumped it and left?

00:39:15.728 --> 00:39:19.168
First, let's request assistance from the highway patrol and local precincts

00:39:19.168 --> 00:39:20.832
And set up checkpoints around the exits and entrances.

00:39:20.832 --> 00:39:23.183
We also need to secure the rest area CCTV footage quickly.

00:39:23.183 --> 00:39:25.716
Let's move quickly. We don't have time.

00:39:29.164 --> 00:39:30.752
What?

00:39:30.752 --> 00:39:31.960
Kwon Tae Seong!

00:39:31.960 --> 00:39:33.016
What are you doing here...

00:39:33.016 --> 00:39:35.246
- Ms. Gu, hurry. - Wait, wait!

00:39:35.246 --> 00:39:37.052
- Don't touch it. - Hey, hey!

00:39:37.052 --> 00:39:38.583
Move the camera away, please.

00:39:38.583 --> 00:39:40.349
Hold on.

00:39:40.349 --> 00:39:42.083
Hey!

00:39:42.709 --> 00:39:45.025
Were you tailing me? Since when?

00:39:45.025 --> 00:39:46.828
Tailing? I just ran into you at the rest area by chance.

00:39:46.828 --> 00:39:49.916
I'm on my way back from covering Pyo Kyu Cheol's release.

00:39:49.916 --> 00:39:52.912
You lost Pyo Kyu Cheol, right? Huh?

00:39:52.912 --> 00:39:55.408
Is this related to Kingfisher?

00:39:55.408 --> 00:39:56.472
What?

00:39:56.472 --> 00:40:00.224
The Kingfisher detective is at the scene where they lost Pyo Kyu Cheol.

00:40:00.224 --> 00:40:03.116
It's not even your jurisdiction. You're a detective from Seoul.

00:40:03.951 --> 00:40:05.616
How do you have such good instincts?

00:40:05.616 --> 00:40:08.049
What's going on?

00:40:08.049 --> 00:40:09.783
Hey, this is...

00:40:10.616 --> 00:40:13.268
I'm only speculating at this point.

00:40:13.268 --> 00:40:15.060
I came here thinking he might be the next target,

00:40:15.060 --> 00:40:16.236
But we got blindsided too.

00:40:16.236 --> 00:40:17.944
We need to find Pyo Kyu Cheol's whereabouts first,

00:40:17.944 --> 00:40:19.849
Whether he's dead or alive.

00:40:19.849 --> 00:40:22.226
Are you saying he might be dead?

00:40:22.226 --> 00:40:25.183
Don't jump to conclusions. He could've just escaped.

00:40:25.183 --> 00:40:26.668
I'm busy, so just go on your way.

00:40:26.668 --> 00:40:28.448
You really can't do this.

00:40:28.448 --> 00:40:31.470
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong, we're refusing your coverage from now on.

00:40:31.470 --> 00:40:33.283
Leave now.

00:40:33.283 --> 00:40:34.449
Don't take pictures!

00:40:34.449 --> 00:40:36.516
- Pack it up now. - Okay.

00:40:39.716 --> 00:40:41.760
<i>The police have started moving.</i>

00:40:41.760 --> 00:40:44.316
They're conducting checkpoints at the tollgate 20 kilometers ahead.

00:40:46.698 --> 00:40:48.420
You should get off the road now.

00:40:48.420 --> 00:40:50.704
Okay, let's take another route.

00:40:50.704 --> 00:40:52.449
Alright.

00:40:56.168 --> 00:40:57.238
Mommy will try it first.

00:41:01.544 --> 00:41:03.416
Yum, it's good!

00:41:07.124 --> 00:41:08.175
Is it tasty, sweetie?

00:41:08.175 --> 00:41:10.507
Yeah! It's super, super delicious!

00:41:10.507 --> 00:41:12.404
- Really? - Yeah!

00:41:12.404 --> 00:41:15.018
You're in the best mood today, huh?

00:41:15.018 --> 00:41:16.076
Were you happy Mommy came?

00:41:16.076 --> 00:41:19.083
Yeah! I was so, so happy!

00:41:19.083 --> 00:41:23.016
Then I should just quit going to work and stay by your side every day, right?

00:41:23.016 --> 00:41:25.772
Well... No. You should work.

00:41:25.772 --> 00:41:28.636
Huh? I should work? Why?

00:41:28.636 --> 00:41:30.883
Because it's a necessary job.

00:41:31.960 --> 00:41:33.660
Huh?

00:41:36.222 --> 00:41:39.189
Daddy hasn't finished all his work yet.

00:41:39.189 --> 00:41:40.249
Should I sing you a song?

00:41:40.249 --> 00:41:42.172
What kind of work?

00:41:42.172 --> 00:41:46.400
Daddy is doing... something very, very important.

00:41:46.400 --> 00:41:50.916
He is a truly good man who does wonderful things for people.

00:41:50.916 --> 00:41:52.271
What about you?

00:41:52.271 --> 00:41:53.449
Huh?

00:41:53.449 --> 00:41:55.916
What do you do?

00:41:57.444 --> 00:41:59.683
I do...

00:42:04.868 --> 00:42:06.044
Something necessary.

00:42:06.044 --> 00:42:07.744
Something necessary?

00:42:08.800 --> 00:42:10.516
Yeah.

00:42:12.072 --> 00:42:14.249
Something the world needs.

00:42:17.916 --> 00:42:20.416
Oh, my smart little girl.

00:42:53.749 --> 00:42:55.883
[Child on Board]

00:43:38.652 --> 00:43:40.549
We shouldn't have come here.

00:43:54.992 --> 00:43:56.116
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:43:56.116 --> 00:43:57.816
Team Leader!

00:44:21.883 --> 00:44:23.216
Move, hurry!

00:44:23.216 --> 00:44:24.949
Hurry!

00:44:32.636 --> 00:44:34.583
Team Leader, are you okay?

00:44:41.370 --> 00:44:43.149
Team Leader, are you okay?

00:44:43.149 --> 00:44:44.836
I'm fine.

00:44:44.836 --> 00:44:46.041
What about Pyo Kyu Cheol?

00:44:46.041 --> 00:44:48.183
We'll have to put things on hold because of the witness issue.

00:44:48.183 --> 00:44:49.916
Catch Pyo Kyu Cheol quickly.

00:44:49.916 --> 00:44:51.469
- Catch him! - Yes.

00:44:51.469 --> 00:44:55.216
Team Leader, you keep bleeding. What should we do about your wound?

00:44:55.216 --> 00:44:57.249
- Oh, no. - What should we do?

00:45:01.996 --> 00:45:03.883
Pull over! Stop the car!

00:45:08.423 --> 00:45:09.656
Do Woon, no!

00:45:09.656 --> 00:45:11.812
Do Woon! Do Woon!

00:45:11.812 --> 00:45:15.524
- I'm Pyo Kyu Cheol, you punks! - Do Woon!

00:45:16.149 --> 00:45:19.149
Which mom, which dad told them to kill me? Huh?

00:45:19.149 --> 00:45:23.283
I'm perfectly alive! What is wrong with you all?

00:45:23.283 --> 00:45:25.516
You punks!

00:45:27.283 --> 00:45:29.000
Mommy...

00:45:29.000 --> 00:45:30.784
Who is this punk?

00:45:30.784 --> 00:45:33.736
Mommy...

00:45:33.736 --> 00:45:36.349
Do Woon!

00:45:38.120 --> 00:45:39.364
- <i>Team Leader.</i> - Yeah.

00:45:39.364 --> 00:45:41.149
<i>Are you okay to drive?</i>

00:45:43.683 --> 00:45:45.420
Yeah, I'm still fine.

00:45:45.420 --> 00:45:47.383
Did you find Pyo Kyu Cheol?

00:45:48.188 --> 00:45:49.888
These punks...

00:45:52.220 --> 00:45:53.984
This punk hasn't been answering his phone for a while.

00:45:53.984 --> 00:45:56.249
Answer the phone!

00:45:59.055 --> 00:46:01.049
What is this now?

00:46:03.649 --> 00:46:06.002
That punk...

00:46:06.002 --> 00:46:07.716
He couldn't have gotten far.

00:46:07.716 --> 00:46:09.980
Can you confirm the GPS location?

00:46:09.980 --> 00:46:11.680
Yes, I can.

00:46:14.364 --> 00:46:16.292
Looks like he's heading toward Incheon.

00:46:16.292 --> 00:46:18.725
He may be trying to catch a boat.

00:46:18.725 --> 00:46:19.725
What is this?

00:46:19.725 --> 00:46:22.549
What now? What is it?

00:46:23.403 --> 00:46:26.149
Jeez, that punk seriously...

00:46:27.232 --> 00:46:29.096
Mommy, I want gummies too. Gummies.

00:46:29.096 --> 00:46:32.650
Huh? Yul, but the doctor said that

00:46:32.650 --> 00:46:36.336
If you eat too many of those, lots of bacteria will grow in your mouth.

00:46:36.336 --> 00:46:38.915
Then you'll have to go to the dentist again. Are you okay with that?

00:46:38.915 --> 00:46:41.143
- No! - You don't want that, right?

00:46:41.143 --> 00:46:44.744
Then how about we grill some fish together today?

00:46:44.744 --> 00:46:46.384
How about mackerel, your favorite?

00:46:46.384 --> 00:46:47.616
I like mackerel!

00:46:47.616 --> 00:46:49.016
- Yul, this is mackerel... - <i>This is a breaking news alert.</i>

00:46:49.016 --> 00:46:53.516
<i>Child sex offender Pyo Kyu Cheol, released today after 16 years in prison,</i>

00:46:53.516 --> 00:46:57.864
<i>escaped during transfer after removing his electronic ankle monitor.</i>

00:46:57.864 --> 00:47:02.122
<i>While police search for him after issuing an emergency wanted notice,</i>

00:47:02.122 --> 00:47:03.144
[Vehicle Stolen, 3-Year-Old Boy] <i>it has been confirmed that</i>

00:47:03.144 --> 00:47:04.496
[Taken Hostage Inside] <i>Mr. Pyo stole a passing vehicle</i>

00:47:04.496 --> 00:47:06.264
- <i>and is fleeing with</i> - Want mackerel?

00:47:06.264 --> 00:47:08.491
- <i>a three-year-old boy as a hostage.</i> - Shall we go?

00:47:08.491 --> 00:47:12.312
<i>Police have found evidence that Mr. Pyo attempted to make a call</i>

00:47:12.312 --> 00:47:15.032
- <i>using the vehicle owner's phone...</i> - The police told us to come here.

00:47:15.032 --> 00:47:16.160
Is the child safe?

00:47:16.160 --> 00:47:18.649
Probation officers, please at least let us know the current location.

00:47:18.649 --> 00:47:19.880
We can't find out either.

00:47:19.880 --> 00:47:21.583
This makes no sense!

00:47:21.583 --> 00:47:23.283
We're sorry.

00:47:27.260 --> 00:47:29.724
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]

00:47:29.724 --> 00:47:33.716
Sir, we haven't gotten much on this side either.

00:47:34.749 --> 00:47:37.330
That punk, if he was going to run, he should've gone alone.

00:47:37.330 --> 00:47:38.428
Why take a child?

00:47:38.428 --> 00:47:40.536
I'll find out what's happening through my police contacts.

00:47:40.536 --> 00:47:43.512
Ms. Gu, go back and look into the information.

00:47:43.512 --> 00:47:45.212
What?

00:47:47.412 --> 00:47:50.516
Mommy.

00:47:51.484 --> 00:47:54.746
Darn it! These persistent punks!

00:47:54.746 --> 00:47:56.649
You all know the priority, right?

00:47:56.649 --> 00:47:58.720
The child's safety comes first, so...

00:47:58.720 --> 00:48:02.216
<i>don't get too close or provoke him.</i>

00:48:02.216 --> 00:48:04.649
<i>Wait for the right opportunity and take him down.</i>

00:48:04.649 --> 00:48:05.816
<i>Got it?</i>

00:48:05.816 --> 00:48:07.549
Yes.

00:48:08.449 --> 00:48:11.072
Keep quiet, you punk! Shut your mouth!

00:48:11.072 --> 00:48:15.410
Mommy.

00:48:32.348 --> 00:48:33.449
That punk, seriously.

00:48:33.449 --> 00:48:35.183
[Child on Board]

00:48:35.968 --> 00:48:37.916
Is he insane?

00:49:06.349 --> 00:49:08.349
[Bo Na]

00:49:13.538 --> 00:49:15.683
Mommy!

00:49:16.412 --> 00:49:17.704
Tae Min!

00:49:17.704 --> 00:49:19.949
Catch that punk!

00:49:25.216 --> 00:49:27.428
Hyun Nam, what about the child?

00:49:27.428 --> 00:49:28.952
Luckily, he doesn't seem injured.

00:49:28.952 --> 00:49:31.472
I'll take him to the car and lay him down first.

00:49:31.472 --> 00:49:33.172
Let's go.

00:49:34.249 --> 00:49:36.083
Mommy...

00:50:14.806 --> 00:50:17.649
Ah, why? Come closer, come closer.

00:50:17.649 --> 00:50:19.282
Come closer, come closer!

00:50:19.282 --> 00:50:22.325
Why aren't you coming? Come here!

00:50:23.420 --> 00:50:26.580
You punks, you all thought I was a pushover.

00:50:26.580 --> 00:50:27.756
Try to kill me!

00:50:27.756 --> 00:50:29.516
Go ahead, try!

00:50:29.516 --> 00:50:33.476
I said kill me, you punks!

00:50:33.476 --> 00:50:36.283
I'm leaving!

00:51:02.348 --> 00:51:04.048
Meeting concluded.

00:51:19.316 --> 00:51:23.301
<i>Bo Na actually doesn't like seeing blood.</i>

00:51:23.301 --> 00:51:28.020
She also hates watching someone die painfully right in front of her.

00:51:28.020 --> 00:51:30.349
That's why she prefers sniping.

00:51:30.349 --> 00:51:34.216
<i>She doesn't have to confront them up close,</i>

00:51:34.216 --> 00:51:36.015
<i>and it's not a method</i>

00:51:36.015 --> 00:51:40.392
<i>that involves unnecessary cruelty, violence, or suffering.</i>

00:51:40.392 --> 00:51:45.308
It's only meant to make them disappear from this world.

00:51:45.308 --> 00:51:47.283
The 'white' cases have been added too.

00:51:49.416 --> 00:51:53.183
<i>But people who hurt children were exceptions.</i>

00:51:53.183 --> 00:51:56.936
<i>That's why other team members handled them until now.</i>

00:51:56.936 --> 00:51:58.315
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:51:58.315 --> 00:52:01.058
<i>Maybe she thought it was too easy a death,</i>

00:52:01.058 --> 00:52:05.383
<i>or maybe there was another reason.</i>

00:52:12.504 --> 00:52:14.349
<i>Anyway, today...</i>

00:52:15.516 --> 00:52:18.283
<i>in the end, Bo Na was the one who ended it.</i>

00:52:36.616 --> 00:52:38.152
[Not Today]

00:52:38.152 --> 00:52:40.600
They all died? How?

00:52:40.600 --> 00:52:44.892
[Summary of Subject Investigation] Car accidents, falls, drownings.

00:52:44.892 --> 00:52:46.336
Another car accident?

00:52:46.336 --> 00:52:48.516
Wow, there's even electrocution.

00:52:48.516 --> 00:52:50.184
And what's strange is that

00:52:50.184 --> 00:52:53.783
[Release Date, Death Date] they all died on the day they were released.

00:52:55.280 --> 00:52:57.583
Isn't that strange?

00:52:57.583 --> 00:53:00.649
If they'd been shot to death by Kingfisher, I might understand.

00:53:00.649 --> 00:53:01.738
But how could every single one of them

00:53:01.738 --> 00:53:04.983
Die unexpectedly on the day they were released?

00:53:07.784 --> 00:53:10.249
- Call an ambulance. Now! - Okay.

00:53:10.249 --> 00:53:14.177
You could say he died an unfortunate death.

00:53:14.177 --> 00:53:15.532
He was such a piece of work.

00:53:15.532 --> 00:53:19.683
Honestly, a guy like him getting gunned down by the Kingfisher is just unsurprising.

00:53:19.683 --> 00:53:21.583
[Reporter Choi]

00:53:22.983 --> 00:53:25.583
Reporter Choi, what happened? From the police...

00:53:25.583 --> 00:53:26.616
- <i>Breaking news.</i> - What?

00:53:26.616 --> 00:53:27.949
- <i>After being released today,</i> - Sir...

00:53:27.949 --> 00:53:28.949
- <i>he cut off his electronic</i> - Sir!

00:53:28.949 --> 00:53:30.549
- <i>ankle monitor and fled...</i> - Look over there.

00:53:30.549 --> 00:53:33.483
<i>He was found dead after being shot by a sniper rifle.</i>

00:53:33.483 --> 00:53:35.716
<i>Mr. Pyo abandoned the vehicle he stole and fled,</i>

00:53:35.716 --> 00:53:37.464
[Pyo Kyu Cheol,] <i>but while attempting to escape</i>

00:53:37.464 --> 00:53:38.949
[Shot Dead by Sniper Rifle] <i>on a fishing boat docked nearby,</i>

00:53:38.949 --> 00:53:43.983
<i>he was struck in the head by a bullet, fell into the sea, and was found dead.</i>

00:53:44.760 --> 00:53:45.866
Even the blanket.

00:53:47.904 --> 00:53:49.940
Understood. Please make sure the area is properly controlled.

00:53:49.940 --> 00:53:51.640
Thank you.

00:53:52.835 --> 00:53:54.449
Sir!

00:53:54.449 --> 00:53:56.592
The child was safely returned to his parents.

00:53:56.592 --> 00:53:59.046
They said he was lying on a sofa in the management office,

00:53:59.046 --> 00:54:00.483
Covered with a blanket.

00:54:00.483 --> 00:54:02.216
That's a relief.

00:54:04.804 --> 00:54:06.683
What's this really?

00:54:06.683 --> 00:54:09.316
It wasn't an accident, and if it was a sniper shot, then this...

00:54:11.883 --> 00:54:13.949
I really don't know.

00:54:15.248 --> 00:54:19.683
Whether we were completely off track or if we actually found the right answer.

00:54:23.280 --> 00:54:25.724
<i>I really feel sorry for Director Yoo.</i>

00:54:25.724 --> 00:54:28.508
We should've handled it somehow,

00:54:28.508 --> 00:54:32.500
But instead we made her the target of the police again.

00:54:32.500 --> 00:54:36.436
A sniper shot can't really be disguised as an accident.

00:54:36.436 --> 00:54:38.458
The bullet leaves evidence behind.

00:54:38.458 --> 00:54:40.983
Like Kingfisher's signature.

00:54:43.106 --> 00:54:46.040
Just hold on a little longer. It's almost done.

00:54:46.040 --> 00:54:48.583
It's ironic, isn't it?

00:54:48.583 --> 00:54:50.712
That bullet puts Director Yoo in danger,

00:54:50.712 --> 00:54:53.583
But at the same time, it protects all of us.

00:54:53.583 --> 00:54:55.452
What do you mean by that...

00:54:55.452 --> 00:54:57.572
It's acting as a kind of decoy.

00:54:57.572 --> 00:54:59.710
It draws the investigation toward her.

00:54:59.710 --> 00:55:01.638
Because Director Yoo is spectacularly drawing attention

00:55:01.638 --> 00:55:03.140
Under the name Kingfisher.

00:55:03.140 --> 00:55:05.980
So other cases can quietly disappear from the spotlight.

00:55:05.980 --> 00:55:08.540
The Musan case last time was like that too.

00:55:08.540 --> 00:55:11.883
So that puts Director Yoo in the most dangerous position.

00:55:11.883 --> 00:55:14.383
She's also the most likely to get caught.

00:55:14.383 --> 00:55:15.383
Bingo.

00:55:15.383 --> 00:55:19.412
That's why we're all sorry and grateful to Director Yoo.

00:55:19.412 --> 00:55:24.416
But no one else could do what she does.

00:55:24.416 --> 00:55:26.949
She's the most capable among us.

00:55:27.821 --> 00:55:29.521
It's done.

00:55:30.244 --> 00:55:31.944
Good work.

00:55:37.347 --> 00:55:38.412
Here you go.

00:55:39.716 --> 00:55:42.444
Oh, you didn't have to pay this much.

00:55:42.444 --> 00:55:46.082
And you really don't have to be this generous every time.

00:55:46.082 --> 00:55:49.716
You rushed over from the library while writing your thesis.

00:55:49.716 --> 00:55:50.844
I feel especially bad today.

00:55:50.844 --> 00:55:54.188
Actually, I was just dozing off.

00:55:54.188 --> 00:55:56.272
Did the matter you went to handle get resolved well?

00:55:56.272 --> 00:55:58.712
The client suddenly filed a complaint, right?

00:55:58.712 --> 00:56:02.504
Thanks to you, it was resolved well. Thank you.

00:56:02.504 --> 00:56:04.284
Mommy!

00:56:04.284 --> 00:56:05.983
Did our Yul wake up?

00:56:05.983 --> 00:56:07.588
Yul!

00:56:07.588 --> 00:56:11.564
She seemed a little down, and then she suddenly fell asleep.

00:56:11.564 --> 00:56:14.080
Really? You did?

00:56:14.080 --> 00:56:17.349
I'm sorry I left when I promised I'd spend today with you.

00:56:18.556 --> 00:56:21.149
You can just give me lots of hugs.

00:56:21.988 --> 00:56:24.088
Of course, I will hug you like this.

00:56:24.088 --> 00:56:26.383
Come on, hug me too.

00:56:28.737 --> 00:56:31.183
How is it, Yul? Do you feel better?

00:56:31.183 --> 00:56:34.649
Yeah, I feel better. What about you?

00:56:35.524 --> 00:56:37.224
Me?

00:56:38.664 --> 00:56:40.483
I'm okay too.

00:56:41.849 --> 00:56:45.516
When I'm holding Yul like this, I'm okay.

00:56:59.088 --> 00:57:01.788
Wow, this time it's a sniper?

00:57:01.788 --> 00:57:03.516
Again on the day of release?

00:57:03.516 --> 00:57:06.283
Sir, what is this?

00:57:07.296 --> 00:57:10.980
This seems to be related to Kingfisher.

00:57:10.980 --> 00:57:13.083
<i>Shouldn't we dig into it?</i>

00:57:41.079 --> 00:57:43.764
The sender's address is from Russia.

00:57:43.764 --> 00:57:46.460
Yeah, it was sent by a friend.

00:57:46.460 --> 00:57:48.383
Yul! Look at this!

00:57:48.383 --> 00:57:51.337
Your mommy's friend sent you a doll as a gift.

00:57:51.337 --> 00:57:54.081
- Yul is lucky. - Wow, it's mine!

00:57:54.081 --> 00:57:55.249
Mommy, give it to me.

00:57:55.249 --> 00:57:57.345
Here.

00:57:57.345 --> 00:57:59.804
It's mine!

00:57:59.804 --> 00:58:01.504
Cute.

00:58:05.096 --> 00:58:07.748
Oh, these are Russian letters.

00:58:07.748 --> 00:58:10.076
What does it say, Bo Na?

00:58:10.076 --> 00:58:11.216
Just a greeting.

00:58:11.216 --> 00:58:14.784
Things like "How have you been?" and "I miss you."

00:58:14.784 --> 00:58:16.398
Oh, I'm jealous.

00:58:16.398 --> 00:58:19.444
You have a friend who even sends you gifts from overseas.

00:58:19.444 --> 00:58:21.916
Indeed, having good friends is nice.

00:59:25.649 --> 00:59:27.663
[Caller ID Restricted: You keep your promises well]

00:59:27.663 --> 00:59:29.683
[Good. Another good night, Tae Seong]

01:00:21.136 --> 01:00:24.279
When did we get a new member of the family without me knowing?

01:00:24.279 --> 01:00:25.883
They sent a gift from Russia.

01:00:25.883 --> 01:00:28.317
They say they'll be coming to Korea soon.

01:00:28.317 --> 01:00:31.136
He's the notorious youngest son of the so-called Royal Family.

01:00:31.136 --> 01:00:32.449
Why were you acting up?

01:00:32.449 --> 01:00:33.728
We need to look into it now.

01:00:33.728 --> 01:00:37.716
Whether it was just an accident or an unjust death disguised as one.

01:00:37.716 --> 01:00:39.916
Anyway, Chairman Cheon Seong Gyu is at the center of it.

01:00:39.916 --> 01:00:43.808
This feels like a terrifying case with a complicated web of connections.

01:00:43.808 --> 01:00:47.380
Sniping isn't the only method Kingfisher uses.

01:00:47.380 --> 01:00:48.616
A joint investigation?

01:00:48.616 --> 01:00:49.846
I'll handle this.

01:00:49.846 --> 01:00:51.508
It's too dangerous for you to be exposed at the scene, Bo Na.

01:00:51.508 --> 01:00:52.508
[Mother]

01:00:52.508 --> 01:00:54.324
- Mother. - It's our family's memorial rite,

01:00:54.324 --> 01:00:55.888
Yet you're making the daughter-in-law do all the work?

01:00:55.888 --> 01:00:57.132
I think this is unfair.

01:00:57.132 --> 01:00:58.832
You little punk...

01:01:00.220 --> 01:01:02.949
Yul! Yul is missing!

